@startuml
title udo — delete(path): unregister node, re-save its parent

actor TUI
participant Tree
participant Persist

TUI -> Tree : delete(path)
Tree -> Tree : (idx, parent) = path.split_last()\n(empty path = root -> Err)
Tree -> Tree : parent.children.remove(idx)\n(parent missing / task / idx out of range -> Err)
Tree -> Tree : fix_cursor_after_remove(parent, idx)
Tree -> Persist : save(parent)\n(parent file drops the child dir / task row)
Persist --> Tree : Ok
Tree --> TUI : Ok

note right of Tree
  **Nothing is deleted on disk.**
  A container's dir and its .udo.toml stay;
  the node is only unregistered from its parent.

  Cursor fix-up (siblings shift left):
  - cursor on later sibling (or inside) → index - 1
  - cursor on removed node (or inside) →
    sibling now at idx, else previous, else parent
  - earlier sibling / other branch → unchanged
end note

@enduml
